, were examined during the present study. The new species can be distinguished from S. angusticollis by the following character states: frons uniformly blackish brown (yellow in anterior quarter or third in S. angusticollis); antennal arista blackish brown (yellowish brown in S. angusticollis); basisternum dark brown (vs. yellow or with paired yellow spots in S. angusticollis); apical spot and median transverse band on wing much darkened in cell r 2 + 3 (such patterns uniform in color in S. angusticollis). The male genitalia of S. angusticollis have not been studied in detail. The difference in male genital characters between these two species needs to be checked in the future.","","text","",""]]},"V6GX":{"d":[["Sichuan","","text","",""]]},"V6H7":{"d":[["PK","PK","iso","",""]]},"V9ZVL":{"d":[["","MX","iso","",""]]},"ZLNW":{"d":[["Cape York","32421","mrgid","",""]]}}